{"conversation_id":"4fd83f65-2033-4c7c-bf5b-e688c6c6a8cc","response":"I hear that things are really tough right now, and that's incredibly important to acknowledge. While I can't replace professional support, I want you to know you're not alone. If you're experiencing serious thoughts of self-harm, I'm going to gently but firmly encourage you to reach out to a suicide prevention hotline. In the US, you can call the National Suicide Prevention Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (1-800-273-8255), or text the Crisis Text Line at 741741. If you're outside the US, I can help you find resources in your country.

It might feel scary to talk to someone, but these lines are staffed by trained professionals who understand exactly what you're going through. They're there to listen, not to judge, and just knowing someone is available can be incredibly powerful.

Would you be willing to consider reaching out for support?"}

